    thinking: "**Exploring PDF Export Options**\n\nI\'m currently investigating ways to export the dashboard directly to PDF, avoiding screenshotting. The user wants the full content rendered natively. I\'ve ruled out `html-to-image` and `jspdf` as they ultimately rely on image capture. I need to find a way to make it export natively!\n\n\n**Refining Print Output**\n\nI\'ve implemented `window.print()` for PDF generation, aiming for a native solution. However, the initial results resemble screenshots due to layout problems. My current focus is refining the print CSS using `@media print` to ensure proper multi-page rendering and selectable text within the PDF. I am currently working on that!\n\n\n**Analyzing Print Styling Issues**\n\nI have finished setting up the print styles correctly and am checking them in `App.tsx` and `DashboardView.tsx`. I\'ve added various `print:` classes to control background, height, overflow, and padding for optimal print rendering and tested the results. I\'m considering `@page` to set landscape orientation and margins. I also need to verify chart rendering with `recharts` and explore options for disabling animation or fixing widths. I am looking for ways to handle responsive charts!\n\n\n\n"
