  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Layout Order**\n\nI\'ve realized the print engine\'s logic. The Business Intelligence Row, positioned last in the screenshot, confirms the print engine\'s processing order. It seems to have a specific page-fitting strategy. The row\'s perfect fit at the page bottom hints that it\'s prioritized for placement, leaving the top cards for overflow if needed.\n\n\n**Investigating Page Breaks**\n\nI\'m puzzled, the print engine isn\'t breaking to the next page, even though the content container lacks a fixed height. The `h-screen` class in `App.tsx` seems to be the culprit. I am wondering, does Tailwind\'s `print:h-auto` truly function as expected? I need to verify that the CSS is properly generated. I have already set `html`, `body`, and `#root` to `height: auto !important;` in `index.css`, and I am overriding flex with `display: block !important;` and `height: auto !important;` for `.flex.h-screen`. There is also `#root` in `index.html`. Maybe the CSS or page breaks is not the key, as the user could have hit \"Save as PDF\" and gotten only 1 page.\n\n\n**Unraveling Flexbox Constraints**\n\nI\'m revisiting the flexbox structure. The `flex-1` in `DashboardView` seems like a red herring because the parent is now `print:block`, so `flex-1` is irrelevant. However, the root cause is the parent\'s parent, the `div` in `App.tsx`, which was set to `h-screen`, and is now overridden by `print:h-auto print:block`. I am looking at `#root`, which is the direct parent of that div. I forced `#root` to `height: auto`, which should propagate, and am now inspecting the effects in the print rendering.\n\n\n**Refining Print Overrides**\n\nI\'m now focusing on overriding height and display. To ensure proper printing, I\'ve implemented a comprehensive strategy in `index.css`. I\'ve overridden heights and displays for numerous elements, including `html`, `body`, `#root`, and various flex and overflow classes to `height: auto !important`, and `overflow: visible !important`. The current aim is to eliminate any potential clipping issues. I\'m also ensuring the page size and margins are defined.\n\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 16
      nanos: 741039085
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
