 a simple rendering inefficiency.\n\n\n**Pinpointing Possible Culprits**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on a potential culprit: the `recharts` `CustomTooltip`. Specifically, I am investigating whether the `Tooltip` component, which includes a `formatter` function, is the root cause. My concern centers on the possibility of `recharts` attempting to clone the payload, which might contain problematic circular references. I\'m focusing my attention on how the `monthlyTrendData` is being handled within the `DashboardView.tsx` `Tooltip` component.\n\n\n**Identifying Export Limitations**\n\nI\'ve just considered a new avenue: the file export functionality. The use of `XLSX.utils.json_to_sheet` within `DashboardView.tsx` with a potentially large `exportData` might be triggering the memory issues. This could be where the clone error originates. I\'m focusing on whether this part of the process is the problem. Also, I searched the codebase and found no usage of `performance.measure`. I\'m now thinking I should research the React 18 issue on DataCloneError mentioned.\n\n\n"
