  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing File State Issues**\n\nI\'ve discovered an interesting point. I\'m storing a `File` object directly within a React state array, specifically within `messages`, as well as separately in `selectedFile`. The React Profiler and DevTools are failing to clone these `File` objects. This could have some important implications for performance monitoring and debugging in my application.\n\n\n**Investigating Memory Constraints**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on a potential memory issue within the `recharts` tooltips, especially when the user interacts with the dashboard. The \"DataCloneError\" might be triggered by continuous ResizeObserver firings within Recharts, though I\'m still trying to pinpoint the root cause of these firings. I\'m also considering wrapping the charts in `React.memo` or using `ResponsiveContainer` to avoid resize loops. Checking `vite.config.ts` for quick fixes now.\n\n\n**Examining Print Media Behavior**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the interaction between print media queries and screen media, following a user action. The `print:block` CSS rule in `DashboardView` has me thinking. It seems that when a print dialog is initiated and then canceled or completed, the browser switches back to screen media, and the print styles no longer apply. This suggests the \"DataCloneError\" might be resolved by adjusting the print behavior. I\'m checking for the usage of a `CustomTooltip` in `DashboardView.tsx` right now. I\'m also examining the handling of `NaN` or `Infinity` values within the data being visualized.\n\n\n**Debugging Data Handling Issues**\n\nI\'m now investigating potential causes for the \"DataCloneError\" related to data handling. I\'m focusing on calculated values like `growth` in my monthly trend data, and wondering if `Infinity` or `NaN` from these calculations might be the issue, but I don\'t see how that would happen. Also checking the structure of `waterfallData` to see if a very large `totalRev` is the problem. It could also be that a `custom formatter` in Recharts\' `Tooltip` that returns something it doesn\'t understand is the problem.\n\n\n**Pinpointing Large Data Volumes**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on a possible memory issue stemming from the sheer size of `deliveryData` and `poLinesData`. Both seem deeply nested, and each has 10,000 items, and passing them as props to `DashboardView`, I think the React Profiler might be struggling to clone this. It\'s possible the performance profiler is choking on the volume of this data.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 770592268
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
